<h2>1. Payroll, Multi-State HRIS &amp; Global EOR TCO Formula</h2>
<p>We compute 12-month Payroll &amp; HRIS TCO using five explicit cost components:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Base Platform + Per-Employee-Per-Month (PEPM) Spend:</strong> <code>12 × (Base_Monthly + W2_Count × W2_PEPM + Contractor_Count × Contractor_PEPM)</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Multi-State Tax Compliance Surcharges:</strong> <code>12 × max(0, States - 1) × Per_Extra_State_Fee</code> + one-time third-party state tax registration fees (<code>$150–$175/state</code> where applicable vs. <code>$0</code> self-registration on state <code>.gov</code> portals).</li>
  <li><strong>Year-End W-2 &amp; 1099-NEC Filing Fees:</strong> <code>$0</code> on Gusto, OnPay, Rippling, and Deel vs. <code>$65 base + $7.50/form</code> on legacy bureaus (ADP RUN / Paychex Flex).</li>
  <li><strong>Global Employer of Record (EOR) Seat &amp; FX Spread:</strong> <code>12 × EOR_Count × $599</code> + foreign-exchange treasury spread (<code>1.25%–3.0%</code> on gross foreign payroll).</li>
  <li><strong>Statutory Federal &amp; State Tax Baseline (<code>.gov</code>):</strong> <code>7.65%</code> FICA + <code>$42/employee</code> federal FUTA (<code>0.6%</code> on <code>$7,000</code> per IRS Publication 15) + state-specific SUI (<code>$160/emp</code> in AZ up to <code>$1,056/emp</code> in WA and <code>$1,290/emp</code> in NJ).</li>
</ul>

